{
  "text": " Why wouldn't you assess this situation with this deadly virus? We had no representative from the DOH come down and speak with us. There was no protocol other than move these patients to the COVID unit, isolate them for 14 days. Some of them will make it, some of them won't. Treatment was without. They weren't given treatment because they had a positive PCR test. If a person had pneumonia or flu, there's this thing called off labeling. They're no longer allowed to be treated for flu or pneumonia. So they weren't given any antivirals and they weren't given any antibiotics, which would normally fight those things. They were moved to a unit. They were told there was no treatment for them. Whoever made it made it. Whoever didn't, you know, didn't.",
